WEBVTT

NOTE Captions for t2-10-conscious-separation.mp3 — machine-transcribed on-device from the existing audio (SR-472). Not proofread.
NOTE Cues with ids phase-recognise/-regulate/-release/-rise mark where each step begins; js/saferise-poster.js reads them.

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:03.150
It's ending.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.810
Or it hasn't it?

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:09.560
And nothing anyone says about that helps very much right now.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.310
So nothing here is going to tell you.

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:13.800
It was for the best.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.110
Or that it will all make sense later.

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:19.720
Or that you'll be glad down the road.

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:21.910
Nobody knows that yet.

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:26.910
And offering platitudes doesn't change what it feels like sitting here today.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.980
This practice isn't going to fix it.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.530
And it asks very little of you.

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:48.270
When something significant ends, the mind tries to process every detail.

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:56.060
But the body often does something else entirely.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.670
It goes quiet, almost numb.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.750
That flat sensation isn't you failing to grieve?

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.240
Or being heartless.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:12.280
It is your nervous system putting up a soft buffer.

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:21.070
Because feeling the full weight of it all at once is simply too much.

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:31.220
The next few minutes are not about achieving closure or finding peace.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:39.630
They are just a quiet space to sit with what is.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:47.360
Without having to explain it to any one.

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:53.860
Four simple steps.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:01.200
You don't need to keep track or analyze.

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:03.270
I will take you through them.

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:09.580
Before we begin.

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:10.830
Let's see.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:17.780
Without forcing anything,

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:21.290
Can you let your shoulders drop just a quarter of an inch?

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:25.630
Let your weight settle into whatever is supporting you right now.

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:29.230
You didn't have to force it.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:32.720
You are right here held by the surface beneath you.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:43.470
We will start by describing what you are feeling in just one word.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:49.730
Maybe that word is numb.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.930
Maybe it is hollow, heavy or quiet.

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:56.710
You don't have to locate where it sits in your body.

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:02.790
That is often hard here.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:06.380
And not finding it belongs to the state itself.

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:13.810
Not to any failure of attention.

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:22.810
There are two separate things stacked together right now.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.730
There is what has actually happened.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:27.580
The ending itself

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:33.280
And then there is you sitting in a flat overwhelmed state about it.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:41.970
Only one of those needs your attention today.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:49.970
Now we move to regulation.

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:53.850
This is not about trying to cheer up or calm down.

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:56.500
Feeling flat is not too much feeling.

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:57.920
It is too little.

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:00.130
An easy, even breath.

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:01.890
Close to your normal pace

00:04:02.360 --> 00:04:03.600
And warmth at your ch

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:11.320
That is what reaches a shut-down system right now.

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:17.030
Contact comes first

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:19.210
Place a hand over your chest

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:21.060
Or hold your own arm.

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:22.750
Whichever is nearer

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:24.300
Let it stay there.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:27.770
Let the steady warmth and weight transfer through.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:34.440
Now the bread

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:37.610
And it doesn't have to be counted or forced today.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.470
An easy, even breath-boat ways.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:44.040
Nothing pulled out longer than feels natural.

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:45.980
Count it if you can.

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:47.720
Don't if you can

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:50.900
Nothing here needs choosing between.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:52.700
Taughts may come

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:54.980
Memories arguments regrets

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:56.250
They may not.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:58.710
Either one is completely fine.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:07.980
If a memory or thought comes, you don't have to engage it.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:12.710
Imagine it as a leaf floating down a slow river.

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:16.670
You are standing on the bank watching it drift past

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:20.370
You don't need to jump into the water to catch it.

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:22.820
Stay here a little longer

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:27.040
This quiet space is the part people usually cut short.

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:34.310
Because sitting in it feels so unfamiliar

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:36.460
There is the ending itself.

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:37.850
That happened.

00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:39.880
And it stays happened.

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:42.840
And then there is the going back through it.

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:45.110
The point where things turned.

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:47.230
The thing you should have said.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.570
The imaginary version.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.240
Where you both did something differently.

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:53.910
And it held together.

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:01.570
Does that loop ever actually finish?

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:04.540
It doesn't reopen anything in reality.

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:06.710
It just runs in the background.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:09.150
Costing you the entire day.

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:17.280
Landing you right back at the start.

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:18.820
Every single time

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:20.420
The ending stays

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:27.490
But you can put down the constant replaying.

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:30.270
And be clear about what that isn't.

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:33.470
Putting it down isn't accepting it in the sense.

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:35.850
Of finding it acceptable.

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:39.030
It isn't being at peace with what occurred.

00:06:39.570 --> 00:06:41.840
It is simply stopping an argument.

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:44.710
Would something that has already happened

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:48.160
Notice the question running beneath the surface.

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:50.940
Why can't I just get past this?

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:53.580
Put that question down, too.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:00.580
There is a hidden schedule in that sentence.

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:03.980
And no such timeline exists for human grief.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:10.200
Ask instead gently

00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:12.500
What was this protection for?

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:18.950
1. Shutting down is what a body does when it has met more emotional volume
than it can digest.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:26.690
And there is nothing physical to push back against.

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:29.930
It is protective and expensive.

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:37.170
And it will eventually lift.

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:39.940
You don't need the answer right now.

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:46.060
Keep the question softly.

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:48.620
It is worth coming back to.

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:50.050
When you are steadier.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:52.730
Look at where you are in this moment

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:54.360
Hand on your chest

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:57.770
Carrying something that hasn't finished being hard

00:07:58.310 --> 00:07:59.220
This is a lot.

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:01.510
And you are still here anyway.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:11.180
Now bring to mind one tiny gentle action for the next hour.

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:14.990
Not moving on and not fixing the situation.

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:18.450
Just one thing that belongs entirely to you.

00:08:19.070 --> 00:08:21.590
Stepping outside to feel the air on your face

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:23.610
Pouring a warm drink.

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:27.600
Simply resting your eyes without a screen in front of you.

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:29.320
Pick just one

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:36.020
That is where your attention can go next. Once you do it, simply acknowledge
to yourself.

00:08:36.350 --> 00:08:37.810
But you took that step.

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:40.000
One more easy breath.

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:42.580
The same length in and out.

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:44.970
Notice how you are right now

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:54.590
Feeling nothing different is very common here.

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:57.110
And it doesn't mean nothing happened.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:05.940
Take your time getting up

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:08.930
Open your eyes whenever you are ready.

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:12.660
Return to this practice as often as you need to.

00:09:13.090 --> 00:09:14.930
Until you no longer do.
